<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-BHP says year gas output down 6 pct.</title>
<headline>RTRS-BHP says year gas output down 6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Broken Hill Pty Co Ltd (BHP) said on Tuesday gas production for the year to May 31, 1997 was down six percent, while production of oil and condensate was up one percent.  </p>
<p>BHP said gas production for May of 22.2 billion cubic feet was down one percent, while production for the year to date totalled 247.1 billion cubic feet.</p>
<p>Oil and condensate production for May totalled 6.058 million barrels, down seven percent, while production for the year to date totalled 68.946 million barrels.</p>
<p>The slight increase in oil and condensate production for the year to May was due to increased production from the North West Shelf and a full year's production from Liverpool Bay, the company said.  </p>
<p>This was offset by the sale of North American production assets, abandonment of the Skua field in the Timor Sea and natural field decline.</p>
<p>BHP said final quarter production of oil and condensate was influenced by stronger production from Bass Strait, associated with the successful Bream B and West Tuna field development and the Gobia infill drilling programmes.</p>
<p>Gas production for the year to May declined because higher production from Liverpool Bay and other UK assets was offset by the disposal of North American and South American properties.  </p>
